 The 3×3×3 Armillary is formed by right-clicking its central **vanilla Amethyst Block** with the **Wand**. Arrange 13 ingredient blocks on the same height in a 7×7 cross pattern. The exact source export is retained in `data/syntacticwizardry/rituals/armillary_formation.json`.
 
 Relative to the amethyst: four Gold Blocks at the cardinal adjacent positions; four Lapis Blocks on the four inner diagonals; and four Copper Blocks three blocks away along the cardinal axes. The two layers above the central 3×3 must be empty. The world layer below the pattern is not checked. On a valid cast the outer four copper markers are consumed, the eight inner Gold/Lapis blocks turn into bottom Cut Copper Slabs, and the central amethyst becomes the Armillary controller. All ingredients are validated before any world changes. The existing armillary planner and geometry remain unchanged.
+
+### Version 0.3.88 – Underground Gnome Village safety
+
+Gnome villages generate a closed, torch-lit structure with a double-oak-door entry corridor leading to a pre-existing natural cavern. Village candidates lacking a safe nearby dry cavern are skipped. Zombies and skeletons target Gnomes as prey. All Gnome variants are valid targets. Existing Gnome defense and professions remain unchanged.
