 - Room ceilings are three blocks above their floor. Rooms on consecutive levels are separated by five blocks.
 - Villages spawn 8–12 ordinary Gnomes. The existing village population manager establishes one Elder per eight ordinary Gnomes, rounded up. Workstation professions operate unchanged.
 - The provisional 24-block horizontal/12-block vertical village-home search still applies. This change does not yet add structural repair blueprints or retroactive regeneration in existing chunks.
+
+## v0.3.88 safety, hostility and cavern access
+
+- Village worldgen now requires a nearby pre-existing natural, dry cave with a solid floor and at least a small connected open pocket. Cave discovery runs **before** any village blocks are placed, so generated interiors cannot be mistaken for caverns. Village candidates without a suitable cave in the nearby search area are skipped.
+- The lowest communal level gains a new outward, roofed 3-block-wide tunnel with reinforced stone-brick side walls. Its last cells open into the discovered cavern. A set of **two adjacent oak doors**, with upper/lower halves and opposing hinges, closes its inner entrance; a stone jamb fills the third hallway lane.
+- Other village corridors receive solid side walls where they do not intersect rooms/shaft junctions. This seals accidental openings into nearby caves.
+- Corridors have post-construction wall torches every six distinct pathway cells (rather than unreliable provisional torches on exterior cave stone). Every room gets four supported wall torches. Existing recessed shaft Glowstone remains unchanged.
+- Zombies (including subclasses) and all vanilla skeleton variants target Gnomes through the normal AI target-goal selector, while retaining normal player priority. Neutral Gnomes still retaliate and alert village allies when attacked.
+- New generation only. Existing generated villages remain unchanged.
